{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And every plant of the field, etc.</b> He comes to inform us of what He alluded to in the first verse, that He is the Creator of all, in the manner I explained. And He said that the earth did not bring forth its vegetation until HaShem watered it, which is His saying: <b>for He had not caused it to rain</b>, etc. He also informed us that the beasts of the field were a formation (yetzirah), as He said: ״וַיִּיצֶר HaShem, etc., every beast of the field״ (Genesis 2:19) — except that He prepared a golem from the earth just as He prepared the form of man, and the swarming creatures of the waters He also alluded to in His saying ״וְעוֹף הַשָּׁמַיִם,״ and they already said, of blessed memory (Ḥulin 27b), that they were created from the moisture." "<b>Further</b>, the verse intends to say — there is a fine point to examine in the verse, further in His saying, <b>and there was no man</b>: what is the intent of this information? Further, why did He return to say <b>and He formed</b>, etc., <b>dust</b>, etc., when He had already made us hear (Genesis 1:27) ״בְּיוֹם בְּרֹא אֱלֹהִים אָדָם״? And if He came to make us hear that from dust He created him, why was it necessary to repeat the declaration of creation? And He should have added there, in the declaration of creation, and said ״עָפָר מִן הָאֲדָמָה״?" "<b>Now</b> it may be explained based on what they said, of blessed memory (Bereshit Rabbah ch. 14), that the first man was the ḥallah of the world. Until here. From their words it is understood that the world has the law of ḥallah, and our Rabbis taught in chapter 2 of tractate Ḥallah (Ḥalah 2:5), and this is their language: one who separates his ḥallah from flour, etc. — it is not ḥallah. And they taught in chapter 3 (Ḥalah 3:1): ״If one kneads with wheat, etc. — one who eats from it is liable to death,״ until here. Now, there is no existence for the earth to bring forth vegetation from itself except through the watering of the earth, and this is the kneading of the dough. From now on, all vegetation of the earth is forbidden until ḥallah is lifted from it, which is the formation of man — for the earth became obligated in ḥallah, and as long as its ḥallah was not lifted, it is tevel (untithed). And this is what the verse says here: <b>and every plant of the field before it was</b>, etc., <b>and every herb</b>, etc., <b>before it grew</b> — for He did not rain on the third day upon the earth to bring them forth, but the earth became pregnant with them by His utterance, may He be blessed, yet they did not emerge. And the reason is that <b>there was no man</b>, who is the ḥallah of the earth. And He stated the remedy that HaShem made to bring forth the vegetation: an ed would rise from the earth and roll all the dust of the world, as He said: <b>and watered all</b>, etc., <b>and HaShem formed</b>, etc., <b>et the man, dust</b>, etc. — this is the lifting of the ḥallah. Once the entire earth became obligated in ḥallah and HaShem lifted this ḥallah, the entire earth and its vegetation were permitted; and if He had rolled in the water one part of the earth, it would not have left the status of tevel except for the part that was rolled." "And you should know that the dust from which man was fashioned was not the dust of the Garden of Eden but that of the world, as the verse precisely states (Genesis 3:23): ״לַעֲבֹד אֶת הָאֲדָמָה אֲשֶׁר לֻקַּח מִשָּׁם״. But the Garden of Eden did not need to have ḥallah lifted from it and only afterward to bring forth plantings from it, for it is entirely holy (kodesh). And therefore He said: <b>and HaShem planted</b>, etc., <b>a garden in Eden, from the east (mikedem)</b> — meaning, before (kodemand) the creation of man, as they said, of blessed memory (Pesaḥim 54a), and He prepared it for man, who was himself holy ḥallah, to benefit from the holy (kodesh), like a priest eating terumah."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:38:31.859043478Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}